// ---- Darkness as a shader term ---------------------------------------------
//
// RELEASING DARKNESS FROM THE SECTOR. DarkDoom darkens by scaling each
// sector's colour: one multiplier, one room, wall to wall. A four-thousand
// unit hall is exactly as dark at the far end as at your feet, because the
// sector is the smallest thing the system can talk about.
//
// On, the SAME four curves run in the fragment shader against each pixel's own
// light. The arithmetic is untouched -- subtract, compress, cap, deepen, with
// pre-gain before and min-light and post-gain after, all reading the same
// ddz_* cvars they always did. What changes is how often it is asked, and that
// it can then take terms a sector cannot express at all.
//
// It is a MODE rather than a replacement because every one of the eight levels
// was tasted against a per-sector multiply and will not feel identical through
// a per-fragment one. Being able to flip between them on the same map is how
// the new defaults get found -- against something, rather than against memory.
//
// Exactly one of the two runs at a time. Both would apply the curve twice.
server bool gitd_dd_perpixel = false;

// DISTANCE. Darkness deepening with range from the eye. This is the one that
