//
// A band used to be a wash: one flat colour, faded by how strongly the band
// covered each pixel. But the band also knows WHERE each pixel is, and every
// shape that defines a distance implies two tangent coordinates -- so a
// pattern can be drawn in the band's own plane. In a corridor that is a
// lattice standing across the hall and travelling toward you.
//
// SPACING 0 IN AN AXIS MEANS NO LINES IN THAT AXIS. That one rule is why there
// is no separate mode for slats or for a single tripwire -- they are a grid
